A version file named as a minor version that declares, beneath a struct, a
field the prior version accepted through ...: the declaration the help offers
is the field at the primary, by its own name, as it is written there.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		...
	}
}
-- ship/history/0.1.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size?: int
		...
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size?: int
		...
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0215]: meta.size in history/0.1.thema is now int, which does not accept every value of the prior _
 --> history/0.1.thema:4:3
  |
4 |         size?: int
  |         ^^^^
  |
  = note: 0.1 is a minor version, so it must accept all data 0.0 accepts
  = note: history/0.0.thema does not declare meta.size by name, but accepts it through ... or a pattern, so an instance may already hold any value there
  = help: declare it as size?: _ to accept what 0.0 accepted, or rename the file history/1.0.thema
